    "confidence": "high",
    "resolution": "All listed CCs are 7-bit (value range 0-127). Finer resolution is available by other means; see caveats.",
    "receive_channel": "Single channel. Factory default is MIDI Channel 1. CC receive is ON by default. (Not Omni by default.) Set the stress test to MIDI channel 1.",
    "caveats": [
      "This map is compiled from a community-maintained CC table (midi.guide) cross-checked with the Squarp community definition; it is NOT a verbatim copy of an official Novation MIDI implementation chart, which is image-based in the bundled PDF and could not be machine-extracted. Treat individual labels as high-but-not-certified confidence.",
      "Finer-than-7-bit resolution: midi.guide states extra resolution is available via NRPN (14-bit). Separately, the Squarp definition describes a dual-CC scheme where a second CC (offset by +32 from the base CC, e.g. cutoff 29 paired with 61, LFO1 rate 30 paired with 62, osc1 mix 23 paired with 55) extends/biases the range for bipolar parameters. These +32 paired CCs and NRPN numbers are NOT individually verified here and are marked confidence low; do not rely on them without testing on hardware.",
      "CC1 (mod wheel) is the universal MIDI standard and the Peak exposes ModWheel as a modulation-matrix source, so it is safe to send, but it does not appear as a numbered entry in the midi.guide parameter table.",
      "Bank/program selection uses standard MIDI Program Change with Bank Select CC0 (MSB) and CC32 (LSB); the Peak documents Program/Bank Change receive as ON by default, but the exact bank MSB/LSB values per patch bank were not confirmed from an official chart.",
      "Resonance (CC79), the filter overdrive/post-drive (CC36/CC80) and distortion level (CC104) can produce loud or self-oscillating output at high values; clamp or limit when sweeping."
    ],
